# Title: Use NTFS Short Name in Command Line
# ID: dd6b39d9-d9be-4a3b-8fe0-fe3c6a5c1795
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-08-05
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1564.004
# Description: Detect use of the Windows 8.3 short name. Which could be used as a method to avoid command-line detection
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((cmdline:*~1.exe* OR cmdline:*~1.bat* OR cmdline:*~1.msi* OR cmdline:*~1.vbe* OR cmdline:*~1.vbs* OR cmdline:*~1.dll* OR cmdline:*~1.ps1* OR cmdline:*~1.js* OR cmdline:*~1.hta* OR cmdline:*~2.exe* OR cmdline:*~2.bat* OR cmdline:*~2.msi* OR cmdline:*~2.vbe* OR cmdline:*~2.vbs* OR cmdline:*~2.dll* OR cmdline:*~2.ps1* OR cmdline:*~2.js* OR cmdline:*~2.hta*)) AND -((((parent_name:*\\WebEx\\WebexHost.exe OR parent_name:*\\thor\\thor64.exe)) OR (cmdline:*C:\\xampp\\vcredist\\VCREDI~1.EXE*))))
